description:
**File:** rust/lichen-ipv6/src/lib.rs
**Lines:** 503-504

**Issue:**
When the UDP length field claims a value less than 8 (e.g., length=5), the error says "expected 5 bytes, got N" but the actual minimum valid UDP datagram is 8 bytes.

```rust
if length < UDP_HEADER_LEN as u16 || length as usize > buf.len() {
    return Err(TooShort::new(length as usize, buf.len()).into());
}
```

**Trigger:** Malformed UDP header with length field < 8.

**Current behavior:** Error says "expected 5, got 100" which is confusing.
**Expected behavior:** Error should indicate minimum UDP header is 8 bytes.

**Fix:** Split into two checks:
```rust
if length < UDP_HEADER_LEN as u16 {
    return Err(TooShort::new(UDP_HEADER_LEN, length as usize).into());
}
if (length as usize) > buf.len() {
    return Err(TooShort::new(length as usize, buf.len()).into());
}
```
